&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Opportunity Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re seeking a&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Clinical Informatician&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;to serve as a key bridge between clinical expertise and data science. In this advanced role, you’ll apply deep clinical reasoning and informatics expertise to design, evaluate, and optimize data-driven healthcare solutions. You’ll also lead ontology mapping, structured data validation, and annotation quality initiatives supporting our next-generation AI and LLM-enabled healthcare tools.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a remote-first role that may require travel to Boston, MA for new hire onboarding and occasional in-person team meetings and company events.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with clinicians, data scientists, and engineers to design and validate digital health and analytics solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate clinical workflows into structured data and logic for algorithms and quality measurement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead efforts in ontology mapping, terminology management (SNOMED, ICD, LOINC, RxNorm), and interoperability standards (FHIR, HL7).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee labeling and abstraction to ensure model safety, accuracy, and clinical integrity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor junior informaticians and specialists in annotation, data validation, and workflow improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll need:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BSN or related clinical degree with active RN license required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4–6+ years of experience in clinical informatics, analytics, or digital health.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced understanding of clinical data, EHR systems, and data standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with data modeling or AI-driven healthcare products preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master’s degree or informatics certification (RN-BC, CPHIMS, ACHIP, etc.) a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
