&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must-Haves&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of deep data engineering, with a proven trajectory of operating in a Staff, Principal, or Architect capacity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be highly proficient in Python, SQL, and modern AI tools with a strong desire and ability to write code and spin up rapid, validating PoCs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mastery over diverse data modeling languages and paradigms- including Relational, Dimensional, Data Vault 2.0, and Graph/Ontological modeling frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Healthcare standards and compliance expertise: Deep understanding of healthcare interoperability standards (FHIR, HL7) and proven experience architecting HIPAA-compliant data platforms in production environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in modern data platforms and cloud-native architectures, with strong command of AWS data services (S3, Glue, Athena, Redshift, Lake Formation)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of data pipeline orchestration, transformation frameworks (dbt, Airflow), and modern data stack components&lt;/li&gt;
